<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mamluk dynasty (Delhi)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Slave Dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mamluk dynasty, also called the Slave Dynasty, was the first ruling line of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>, from 1206 to 1290. It was founded by Qutb al-Din Aibak, a former slave commander of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-of-ghor">Muhammad of Ghor</a>. Its rulers, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iltutmish">Iltutmish</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balban">Balban</a>, consolidated Muslim rule over northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></div>
